      "text": "Traditional methods like Hidden Markov Model (HMM) with rule based approaches,, and Support Vector Machine (SVM) with manual feature-engineering have been applied but they perform poor compared to neural.\n\nFirst we are comparing BiLSTM, BiLSTM+CNN, BiLSTM+CRF, BiLSTM+CNN+CRF models with CNN model and Stanford CRF model.\n\nSecondly, we show the comparison between models trained on general word embeddings, word embedding + character-level embedding, word embedding + part-of-speech(POS) one-hot encoding and word embedding + grapheme clustered or sub-word embedding.\n\nThis trained model consists of vectors for 72782 unique words.\n\nEvaluation\tIn this section, we present the details regarding evaluation and comparison of our models with other baselines.\n\nWe can deduce that Skip Gram models perform better compared CBOW models for word2vec and fasttext.\n\nHere,\n\nTable TABREF35 shows the model architecture comparison between all the models experimented.\n\nThis model is trained till the current function value is less than $1\\mathrm {e}{-2}$.\n\nWe showed that the word vectors learned through fasttext skip gram model performs better than other word embedding because of its capability to represent sub-word",
